      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Blue Sky Property are delighted to present Dunbin, Knockbridge a spacious four bedroom split-level detached residence set on a stunning private site extending to approx. 1.75 acres of mature nature grounds.\r\n\r\nThis is a rare opportunity to acquire a flexible family home offering generous accommodation throughout, set within mature trees, natural planting and uninterrupted countryside views.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation comprises a large entrance hallway leading to kitchen, dining room, spacious living room and a light-filled conservatory with views over the stunning grounds. \r\n\r\nThe sleeping accommodation is arranged over split levels providing excellent flexibility and comprises 4 bedrooms in total - 2 bedrooms (1 en-suite) on the entrance level and 2 further bedrooms (1 en-suite) on the ground floor, along with main family bathroom and large storeroom / utility.\r\n\r\nExternally the property is approached via a private entrance and is set within its own approx. 1.75 acres of stunning nature grounds with mature trees, lawns, natural hedgerows and total privacy.\r\n\r\nThis property offers huge potential and is ideally suited to those seeking privacy, space and countryside living.\r\n\r\nFor all further information contact Blue Sky Property on 042-9329333. Guide Price €425,000.\r\n\r\nLOCATION \r\nNestled in the heart of the rolling countryside, Dunbin enjoys a truly idyllic and private setting in Knockbridge, surrounded by mature trees, hedgerows and open farmland, the property offers complete tranquility and privacy while remaining exceptionally convenient.\r\n\r\nKnockbridge Village itself, with its highly regarded national school, local shop, church, traditional pub and St Brides Gfc is just a short drive away. The coastal village of Blackrock with its promenade, restaurants and seafront walks is within 10 minutes, while Dundalk Town Centre, with its excellent shopping, secondary schools, train station and Marshes Shopping Centre, is approx. 8km away.\r\n\r\nFor commuters, the M1 Motorway at Castlebellingham is easily accessible, placing Dublin City Centre approx. 1 hour and Belfast approx. 1 hour away. Dundalk Train Station offers direct services to Dublin Connolly.\r\n\r\nThis is countryside living at its finest - peaceful, private, surrounded by nature, yet within minutes of everything you need.\r\n\r\nBlue Sky Property and their servants or agents assume no responsibility for and give no guarantees, undertakings or warranties concerning the accuracy, completeness or up to date nature of the information and do not accept any liability whatsoever arising from any errors or omissions. The information does not constitute or form part of a contract and cannot be relied on as a representation of fact. Subject to contract / contract denied. Please note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate, and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
